{
  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's perception and actuation capabilities, separating sensing (uncontrollable) and motion (controllable) as required. The specification encodes a safe, coverage-oriented supervisor: random_walk is used in clear states, move_forward is used for short progress, and obstacle events force conservative, directed recovery. Recovery from front obstacles uses a short turn; side obstacles use a single directed turn away. full_rotate is only enabled in a dedicated search state after repeated blockage. All transitions are deterministic, and the supervisor quickly returns to exploration after recovery.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for sensing and motion to reflect the robot's hardware and runtime semantics.",
    "Specification automaton encodes safe, coverage-biased exploration: random_walk in clear, move_forward for short progress, directed turn recovery for obstacles, and full_rotate only as a last-resort scan."
  ],
